// One-key patch for the stock US International layout: AE11, the key left of
// Backspace, gets an en dash on the third level.
//
// Unlike ../symbols/de this is not a variant anyone selects.  ../rules/evdev
// appends it whenever layout=us variant=intl is active, in any group, so
// nothing is registered in ../rules/evdev.xml and the Settings dialog is
// unchanged: us(intl) simply behaves differently from now on.
//
// The section deliberately is NOT called 'intl'.  It cannot be.  The stock rule
//     *  *  =  pc+%l%(v)
// turns us+intl into  pc+us(intl), which finds this file first, so a section
// named 'intl' containing  include "us(intl)"  would match itself - the
// recursion libxkbcommon 1.6.0 segfaults on rather than reports (see
// ../symbols/de).  With the section named 'ndash', the name 'intl' stays
// unclaimed here, the include falls through to the stock
// /usr/share/X11/xkb/symbols/us, and rules/evdev appends this section after it.
// Same fall-through that lets symbols/de shadow the German layout safely, so
// every other stock us variant (dvorak, colemak, alt-intl, ...) is untouched
// and keeps tracking upstream.

// Hands plain 'us' back to the stock layout: no section named 'basic' here, so
// the include falls through.  This one has to exist: pc+us (layout without a
// variant) asks for this file's *default* section, and a file whose only
// section were 'ndash' would hand the bare us layout a single key.
default partial alphanumeric_keys
xkb_symbols "passthrough" {
    include "us(basic)"
};

// 'ndash' is the HTML entity name; X11 has no keysym of that name, and an
// unrecognised keysym compiles to NoSymbol with only a warning - which looks
// exactly like the override silently not applying.  The en dash U+2013 is
// 'endash' (keysymdef.h: #define XK_endash 0x0aaa); the explicit form 'U2013'
// works too.  'emdash' (U+2014) is the longer one, if that was meant.
//
// The line respecifies all four levels, so it also drops the dead key that
// stock us(intl) has on level 4:
//     key <AE11> { [ minus, underscore, yen, dead_belowdot ] };
// i.e. yen moves from level 3 to level 4 and dead_belowdot goes away.
//
// No level3() include is needed: us(intl) already pulls in
// level3(ralt_switch), and this section is merged into that keymap.
partial alphanumeric_keys
xkb_symbols "ndash" {
    key <AE11> { [     minus, underscore,  endash,  yen ] };
};
